sequenceDiagram
  actor Organizer
  actor Participant
  participant Host as Authorized event service
  participant DB as Persistent store
  participant Artifacts as Private pinned execution artifacts
  participant Bus as EventBridge event bus
  participant Flow as Step Functions
  participant Runtime as Runtime worker (Docker, Lambda or CodeBuild)
  Note over Host,DB: Local: persistent SQLite; cloud: selected Turso or DynamoDB
  Organizer->>Host: Prepare selected event problems
  Host->>Host: Validate event, team and runtime
  Host->>DB: Retain jobs and ownership
  alt New local Docker event
    Host-->>Organizer: Up to 512 dormant jobs prepared
    Participant->>Host: Start / resume own assigned problem
    Host->>Host: Check event/team access and active/memory limits
    Host->>DB: Persist owned operation and runtime ports
    Host->>Runtime: Create bounded Compose plan or resume existing project
    Runtime-->>Host: Outputs or failure
    Host->>DB: Persist status and private runtime data
    Participant->>Host: Stop (keep data)
    Host->>Runtime: Stop; retain writable layer and volumes, not RAM
    Host->>DB: Persist stopped status and retained runtime ports
  else Cloud AWS problem
    Host->>Host: Require verified competitor account separate from hosting account
    Host->>Artifacts: Resolve event's saved catalogKey and source identity
    Host->>DB: Retain deployment and catalogKey
    Host->>Bus: Publish DeployCreateRequested or BulkDeployCreateRequested
    Host-->>Organizer: Accepted job reference
    Bus->>Flow: Start restored deployment workflow
    alt Lambda deployment path
      Flow->>Runtime: Invoke CfnDeploy and poll DescribeStack
      Runtime->>Artifacts: Read pinned template and metadata; verify content hashes
    else CodeBuild deployment path
      Flow->>Runtime: Start build with saved source ZIP key and VersionId
      Runtime->>Artifacts: Read exact source archive from private source bucket
    end
    Runtime->>Runtime: Assume verified competitor role with required ExternalId
    Runtime->>Runtime: CloudFormation create, update, no-op or recreate
    Flow->>DB: Persist status directly (DynamoDB) or through StatusWriter (Turso)
    Organizer->>Host: Event Teardown before platform removal
    Host->>Bus: Publish DeployDeleteRequested for owned deployments
    Bus->>Flow: Run delete workflow and persist result
  else Native Cryptography Battle
    Host->>DB: Retain pinned plugin identity and native state
    Host-->>Organizer: Ready without Docker or competitor account when score stealing is disabled
  else Legacy local Docker event
    Host->>Runtime: Existing deployment lifecycle
    Runtime-->>Host: Outputs or failure
    Host->>DB: Persist status and private runtime data
  end
  Note over Host,Artifacts: Saved cloud events and deployments keep catalog A after catalog B or removal; unpinned legacy data requires a verified original snapshot
  Note over Host,Runtime: No automatic eviction or reset; synthetic allocation is not a Docker benchmark
  Note over Organizer,Runtime: Ordinary make destroy removes the AWS platform and default owned data; external Turso and the separate source bucket remain. --drain-events is rejected.
